.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH tapectl-volume-deposit 1  "tapectl-volume-deposit " 
.SH NAME
tapectl\-volume\-deposit \- Record and inspect WAREHOUSE DEPOSITS of sealed volumes (ADR\-0006)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtapectl volume deposit\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-y\fR|\fB\-\-yes\fR] [\fB\-\-config\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
Record and inspect WAREHOUSE DEPOSITS of sealed volumes (ADR\-0006).
.PP
tapectl does NOT move the bytes. Issue #72 was rescoped by CTO decision: an operator copies a sealed volume\*(Aqs bytes to cold cloud storage by the documented external procedure (rclone / aws\-cli) and then RECORDS that copy here, so the catalog can reason about it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Output in JSON format
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Show what would be done without making changes
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enable verbose output
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts
.TP
\fB\-\-config\fR \fI<CONFIG>\fR
Path to config file
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
tapectl\-volume\-deposit\-add(1)
Record that a sealed volume\*(Aqs bytes now also exist at a warehouse
.TP
tapectl\-volume\-deposit\-list(1)
List recorded deposits
.TP
tapectl\-volume\-deposit\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
